problems.problem:
Tested on code it was not developed on: tldraw src/lib, BlockNote react and shadcn, react-arborist and @lexical/react (356 TSX files, 52,666 lines). E1s made 41 rule hits: about 10 clear raw literals, about 26 false positives and 5 debatable, so roughly 63% false positives. The false positives come from:
- the property-name selectors matching any object literal: floating-ui options `autoPlacement({ padding: 10 })` and `shift({ padding: 4 })`, schema descriptors `backgroundColor: "string"`, and tldraw's colour enum `color: 'black'` (8 hits);
- the unanchored `^(…fontSize…)` regex matching `fontSizeAdjustment`;
- `bottom: '100%'`, `borderRadius: '50%'` and the off-screen `-10000px` pattern.
The report's held-out set, shadcn, is Tailwind-class code, so it never exercised style objects. The fixture has none of these patterns either.

problems.fix:
Scope the selectors:
- to `JSXAttribute[name.name='style']` object expressions and css()/styled() arguments;
- anchor the regexes with `$`;
- exempt percentages and the visually-hidden idiom.
Ship at warning level. Re-measure on style-object-heavy held-out code (the five codebases above are available in S4's node_modules) before recommending that it block CI.

problems.problem:
About 8 of the 11 are optical nudges of 3 px or less, some sub-pixel: margin-top 3px, margin ±0.5px, inset 1px, padding-bottom 0.5px, margin-right -2px. The categoriser in run-lint.mjs labels any literal without var() 'raw-literal', which conflates 'literal' with 'violation'. On three other token-first stylesheets, CSS-D gave:
- tldraw ui.css: 115 flags in 2,337 lines;
- ckeditor5: 184 flags, after excluding 101 token definitions;
- ag-grid: 146 flags, after excluding 40 token definitions.
Positional properties (top/right/bottom/left/inset) were 23/101, 27/88 and 69/125 of the length flags. Positional values, negative margins and values of 2 px or less together were 45%, 59% and 74%.

s12() solves exactly the measured pairs:
- solidOk checks T1 against both gates;
- a hover colour is accepted only if it passes;
- accentText is solved against bg, surface and the subtle ground (T3–T5) and reused for indicator and focus (N1–N3).
So the WCAG 100% and the non-text 100% are also by construction; only fidelity and Lc 75 are independent. On 1,500 random held-out colours × 2 modes, s12 moved the fill in 37.4% of tenant-modes (median ΔE 5.4 among moved fills, p90 9.5, maximum 40). The medians of 1.75/4.8 on 12 hand-picked tenants understate the typical cost.

These are [K] or [S] judgement written as rules:
- the 64 px target is [K], and the limits section says only weak snippets were found;
- the tile size comes from one Odoo min-height for cards without images;
- only the multipliers for the iterate triggers are marked as judgement, not the rollback thresholds.
'All operable controls' overstates EN 301 549 8.3.2, which requires 'at least one of each type of operable part'; the Findings section states this correctly. EN 301 549 v3.2.1 is not yet a harmonised standard under the EAA.
